To build a small page from a template, structure it with plain HTML and placeholder tags that the converter replaces. [https://example.com/a 1]
Below is a minimal template you can save as an .html file:

{{{#!text/html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>{{title}}</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>{{heading}}</h1>
</body>
</html>
}}}

To adjust it further, tell me:

 * Which kind of document you want to build (for example an invoice or a report)?
 * Which templating syntax your tool needs (for example Mustache or plain HTML)?

Method 1: Using the helper package

The helper package tracks your routes and builds the output. [https://example.com/b 2]

 1. Install the package:

{{{#!sh
pip install helper-package
}}}

 2. Use it in your application:

{{{#!python
# Initialize the extension
helper = Helper()

class Page:
    def render(self):
        if __name__ == "__main__":
            return "Home"

    # a trailing comment
}}}

Best Practices

 * Keep the names stable.
 * Cache large outputs.
